  narrativeCategory: 0
  dialogueLines:
  - subtitleText: In December 1944, Josef Kramer, later dubbed the 'Beast of Belsen',
      took command of the camp. Under his rule, tens of thousands of prisoners from
      evacuated camps were brought here. He did nothing to provide adequate food,
      water, or sanitation, causing catastrophic outbreaks of typhus and starvation.
